"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","temperature_C":37,"doi":"10.1021/acs.jmedchem.6c00108","year":2026,"record_id":"MLDB-002510","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The octanol–water partition coefficient (log Pow_{ow}ow) was determined using the shake-flask method combined with UV–vis analysis, a standard approach to evaluate lipophilicity and predict membrane permeability. (107,108) Approximately 10 mg of complex was dissolved in a biphasic system containing equal volumes (1 mL each) of water and 1-octanol. The mixture was agitated at 1000 rpm for 24 h at 37 °C to reach equilibrium. After centrifugation at 15,000 rpm for 15 min, the organic and aqueous layers were separated, and the concentration of the complex in each phase was determined spectrophotometrically. Log P was calculated as LogP=[Complex]octanol/=[Complex]water. Each experiment was repeated three times to ensure reproducibility."}]}